MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The last two attempts fixed model discovery and then getModelOptions(), and
neither changed what /model shows. /model builds its own option list and passes
it as `optionsOverride`, which the picker uses *instead of* getModelOptions() —
the source even says so ("The picker renders `optionsOverride ?? getModelOptions()`").
So both fixes sat on a path this command never takes.

Apply it at `modelOptionsBase`, the single point where the override and the
default list converge, so every picker entry point is covered: /model, the
prompt hotkey, and Settings.

25 rows with generic descriptions → 11 rows described by how each model is
actually served.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
